  "reason": "The proposed link 'Memorizing dataset specific noise' -> 'improved training performance' via 'leads_to' is factually incorrect in the context of overfitting. While memorization often results in high training accuracy (which can be described as improved performance on the training set), the causal chain intended by the seed is that this behavior causes the *failure* to generalize, not just an improvement in training metrics. The original claim conflates the mechanism (memorization) with the outcome (generalization failure). A sound correction must explicitly link 'Memorizing dataset-specific noise' directly to the definition of overfitting or the specific failure condition ('improved training performance fails to translate into performance on unseen examples') rather than an intermediate and potentially misleading state of 'improved training performance' alone. The corrected fact should assert that memorization is a cause of the phenomenon defined as overfitting.",
